# =====================================================================
# Defense-in-depth for local/XAMPP-style deployments where Apache's
# DocumentRoot is the generic htdocs folder rather than this project's
# public/ subfolder (see README: "Point your web server document root
# at /public"). Without a dedicated vhost, everything under this
# project directory is otherwise reachable over HTTP.
#
# Confirmed exploitable before this fix: database/database.sql,
# database/backups/*.sql (contains password hashes + applicant PII),
# config/database.php, includes/*.php, and .git/ internals were all
# directly downloadable, and Apache's default "Options Indexes" served
# a browsable directory listing of database/.
#
# The directory-specific .htaccess files (database/, includes/,
# config/, resources/, node_modules/, .git/) deny access outright.
# This root file adds a project-wide fallback: no directory listings,
# and no dotfiles or backup/dump/log/config extensions served directly,
# in case a sensitive file is ever added somewhere not already covered.
#
# For a production deployment, point the vhost's DocumentRoot at
# public/ directly (per README) — that is the primary fix; this file
# is a safety net, not a substitute for it.
# =====================================================================

Options -Indexes

<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    <FilesMatch "(?i)(^\.|\.(sql|bak|old|backup|log|env|ini|json|lock|md)$)">
        Require all denied
    </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    <FilesMatch "(?i)(^\.|\.(sql|bak|old|backup|log|env|ini|json|lock|md)$)">
        Order deny,allow
        Deny from all
    </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
